{"id":"tk-rev-01","text":"Review this GS statement excerpt for the AU Genuine Student requirement and tell me what to fix: \"I completed my BBS from a campus in Kathmandu in 2022. After that I stayed at home and helped my family. I have always dreamed to study in Australia because it is a developed country with world class education and multicultural society. I chose Master of Business Administration at a university in Sydney because it is very good university and the course will help me to get good job. After completing my study I will return to Nepal and serve my country. My father is a businessman and he will support all my expenses.\" He's 27, gap 2022–2026.","intent":"document_preparation","task":"review","destinations":["australia"],"mode":"single","origin":"nepal","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-02","text":"Review these mock answers a Vadodara student gave for her UK credibility interview and flag what would worry the officer: \"Q: Why this university? A: It is ranked well and my friend also studies there. Q: Why not study in India? A: Indian degrees are not valued. Q: Who pays? A: My father, he has savings. Q: How much is your tuition? A: Around 15 or 16 thousand pounds I think. Q: Plans after? A: I will do the Graduate Route and get experience, then decide.\" She's doing an MSc in International Business at a university in Birmingham.","intent":"visa_risk_analysis","task":"review","destinations":["united_kingdom"],"mode":"single","origin":"india","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-03","text":"Review this practice F-1 interview transcript for a Dhaka student (BS in Computer Science, a state university in Kansas) and tell me where he's weak: \"Officer: Why this university? Student: Because it gave me admission and the fees are low. Officer: Who is sponsoring you? Student: My uncle in New York and my father. Officer: What does your father do? Student: Business. Officer: What business? Student: He has shops. Officer: What will you do after graduation? Student: I will see, maybe work some years there.\"","intent":"visa_risk_analysis","task":"review","destinations":["united_states"],"mode":"single","origin":"bangladesh","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-04","text":"Review this sponsor letter (translated from Vietnamese) for a 500 application and tell me if Home Affairs will find it convincing: \"I, the undersigned, am the aunt of the applicant. I own a coffee shop in Bien Hoa with stable income. I commit to pay all tuition and living costs for my niece for 2 years in Australia. Attached is my savings book with 1.2 billion VND deposited on 3 September.\" The student's parents are farmers; the aunt is unmarried.","intent":"financial_viability","accept":["document_preparation"],"task":"review","destinations":["australia"],"mode":"single","origin":"vietnam","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-05","text":"Review this study plan / letter of explanation for a Canadian study permit and list what an officer would question: \"I graduated BS Psychology in 2017 and worked as a call centre agent for 6 years. I want to study Early Childhood Education diploma in Winnipeg because there is a big demand in Canada and I love children. My savings is enough for my study. After my studies I will come back to the Philippines and open a daycare center.\" Applicant is 30, from Bacolod.","intent":"document_preparation","accept":["visa_risk_analysis"],"task":"review","destinations":["canada"],"mode":"single","origin":"philippines","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-06","text":"Review this cover letter for an NZ student visa (Thai applicant, 29, from Phuket, applying for a Graduate Diploma in Tourism Management in Queenstown): \"Dear Visa Officer, I am writing to explain my purpose of study. I graduated with a Bachelor of Arts in English from a university in Songkhla in 2018. Since then I have worked in a hotel front office for 5 years and was promoted to shift leader last year. Tourism in Phuket is recovering and many hotels want staff with international qualifications. New Zealand is a beautiful country and I enjoyed the movies filmed there. I would like to improve my skills in New Zealand which is famous for tourism. My parents own a guesthouse and they will pay for me. After study I will go back to Thailand to manage the family business.\" What's missing or risky?","intent":"document_preparation","task":"review","destinations":["new_zealand"],"mode":"single","origin":"thailand","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-07","text":"Check this financial summary I prepared for a Colombo student's 500 (Master of Engineering, Melbourne, tuition AUD 46,000/yr) and tell me if it meets the requirement: \"Funds shown: Father's FD LKR 9,500,000 (opened 2 weeks ago); Mother's savings LKR 2,100,000; Education loan approval LKR 6,000,000 (in-principle only). Total ≈ AUD 57,000. Living cost assumed: AUD 21,000. Tuition first year: AUD 46,000. Travel: not included.\"","intent":"financial_viability","task":"review","destinations":["australia"],"mode":"single","origin":"sri_lanka","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-08","text":"Review this sponsorship letter for a UK Student visa (Lalitpur student, MSc in Glasgow): \"I, the maternal uncle of the applicant, hereby declare that I will bear all expenses of my nephew's study in the UK. My balance at a commercial bank in Kathmandu is NPR 52,00,000 as per the attached statement dated 1 October 2026.\" Is this usable, and what would you replace it with?","intent":"financial_viability","accept":["document_preparation"],"task":"review","destinations":["united_kingdom"],"mode":"single","origin":"nepal","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-09","text":"Review this financial summary we're sending to a university for an Indian student's I-20 (MS in Mechanical Engineering, Arizona, stated COA USD 58,000): \"Father's savings ₹22 lakh; Provisional loan letter ₹40 lakh (no sanction number); Mother's gold valuation ₹8 lakh; Agricultural land (no valuation).\" Will this be accepted, and what's weak for the visa interview later?","intent":"financial_viability","task":"review","destinations":["united_states"],"mode":"single","origin":"india","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-10","text":"Review this SOP excerpt for a Canadian study permit (Bangladeshi applicant, BBA 2019, applying for a 1-year postgraduate certificate in Project Management in Toronto): \"I completed my BBA in Marketing from a private university in Dhaka in 2019 with CGPA 2.91. After my BBA I worked at a garments buying house as a merchandiser for two years, then I prepared for the BCS exam but was not successful. In 2024 I started helping in my father's real estate office. Project Management will help my career because every company needs project managers. I chose this college because the tuition is affordable and the intake is available. Canada is a peaceful country and my cousin lives there. My father, a retired government officer, will fund me.\" Point out weaknesses and suggest stronger content.","intent":"document_preparation","task":"review","destinations":["canada"],"mode":"single","origin":"bangladesh","review":false}
{"id":"tk-rev-11","text":"Review this UK master's personal statement excerpt from a Hanoi student applying for MSc Marketing (graduated 2021, worked at a cosmetics retailer): \"Marketing is everywhere in our life. Since I was a child I have been fascinated by advertisements on television and the colourful packaging in supermarkets. During my bachelor's in Business Administration I achieved a GPA of 7.2/10 and joined the marketing club. After graduating I worked at a cosmetics retailer for three years, first as a sales assistant and then supporting social media campaigns. I learned that customers in Vietnam are changing very fast because of TikTok. The UK is the home of many famous brands, so I want to study there. I am hard-working and creative.\" How should she restructure it and what's missing for admissions?","intent":"application_process","accept":["document_preparation"],"task":"review","destinations":["united_kingdom"],"mode":"single","origin":"vietnam","review":true}
{"id":"tk-rev-12","text":"Review this GS answer for a Filipino registered nurse (34, from Baguio) doing an ELICOS + Master of Nursing package in Perth: \"I have been a nurse for 11 years in a provincial hospital. I want to upgrade to Master of Nursing because nurses in Australia are respected and well paid. My husband and two kids will stay in the Philippines. I will go back after.\" What would a case officer doubt?","intent":"document_preparation","accept":["visa_risk_analysis"],"task":"review","destinations":["australia"],"mode":"single","origin":"philippines","review":false}
