{"id":"tk-rev-14","text":"Review this study plan for a Sri Lankan engineer (B.Sc. Eng. 2020, Moratuwa) going to an MSc in Aerospace Engineering in the UK: \"I graduated in Mechanical Engineering with a Second Class Upper in 2020. I worked 4 years at a power company as a maintenance engineer, responsible for turbine overhauls and vibration analysis. I have always been interested in aircraft. I want to study aerospace propulsion because Sri Lanka will need aviation engineers in future as the airport expands. The UK has a long history in aerospace and the course has a module on gas turbine performance which connects to my work. After completing my degree I hope to join an MRO company or return to the power sector.\" Apart from the plan's weaknesses, is anything missing from his visa file for this subject?","intent":"document_preparation","task":"review","destinations":["united_kingdom"],"mode":"single","origin":"sri_lanka","review":false}
