{"id":"tk-sum-01","text":"Summarize what changes for my Nepali students from this pasted announcement: \"The Government has set the National Planning Level for 2027 at 295,000 new international student commencements, allocated across universities, VET and non-university higher education providers. Providers exceeding their allocation will face slower visa processing for new applicants under Ministerial Direction. The student visa application charge will be indexed on 1 July. Students already holding a visa and those applying for a course with the same provider are not counted toward the allocation. Transitional arrangements apply to applications lodged before the commencement date.\"","intent":"policy_change","task":"summarize","destinations":["australia"],"mode":"single","origin":"nepal","review":false}
{"id":"tk-sum-02","text":"Summarize for counsellors what this partner-university email means for our Indian MSc applicants: \"Dear partners, following the immigration white paper, the Graduate Route will be reduced to 18 months for applications made on or after 1 January 2027. PhD graduates are unaffected. Students whose Student visa application was lodged before the change remain under existing rules for their own course but will apply under the rules in force when they apply for the Graduate visa. We are also reviewing our Basic Compliance Assessment metrics and will tighten checks on applicants from some regions.\"","intent":"policy_change","task":"summarize","destinations":["united_kingdom"],"mode":"single","origin":"india","review":false}
{"id":"tk-sum-03","text":"Summarize what changes for my Bangladeshi diploma applicants from this pasted IRCC update: \"Most new study permit applicants require a Provincial or Territorial Attestation Letter. Master's and doctoral students are now included in the cap but exempt from the PAL requirement as of 1 January. College graduates must have studied in a field linked to an occupation in long-term shortage to be PGWP-eligible; the field list is updated annually and applies based on the date the study permit application was submitted. Language requirements apply to PGWP applications submitted after 1 November 2024.\"","intent":"policy_change","task":"summarize","destinations":["canada"],"mode":"single","origin":"bangladesh","review":false}
{"id":"tk-sum-04","text":"Summarize this pasted embassy notice for my Vietnamese F-1 students: \"Effective immediately, all nonimmigrant visa applicants must interview in their country of nationality or residence. Interview waiver eligibility is limited to renewals of the same visa category that expired less than 12 months ago. F, M and J applicants must set social media accounts to public. Applicants should expect longer wait times during peak season; expedited appointments are considered only for start dates within 30 days.\" What do they need to do differently?","intent":"policy_change","task":"summarize","destinations":["united_states"],"mode":"single","origin":"vietnam","review":false}
{"id":"tk-sum-05","text":"Summarize what changes for my Filipino students in this pasted INZ update: \"From 3 November 2025, student visa holders with work rights can work up to 25 hours per week during term time. Students who already hold a visa with a 20-hour condition must apply for a variation of conditions to benefit. The minimum living funds required for tertiary students will be reviewed in the next update; the current amount remains in force until a new figure is published.\"","intent":"policy_change","task":"summarize","destinations":["new_zealand"],"mode":"single","origin":"philippines","review":false}
